YAAP Rog-Orc-Mal-Cha
artiwishless

Continuing my alphabetic ascension series, I started playing rogue
orc. I managed to ascend the very first game, but boy, what game it
was: from the beginning very lucky one, but in one terrible mistake it
was almost destroyed. Yet, this was certainly the most exciting game
in my nethacking career.

1) Bought cursed -1 shield of reflection in early shop and wore it
immediately.

2) Backstabbing with thrown daggers worked wonderfully. I was killing
all the difficult monsters I normally run circles around with amazing
ease.

3) I screwed Sokoban badly, so I had to go out for a pick-axe. When I
returned I have found the first wand of wishing. I wished for scrolls
of charging and GDSM.

4) At the top Sokoban level I got soldier with wand of death. Luckily,
I had the shield of reflection, so I got the wand easily.

5) Sokoban gave me bag of holding and also two rings of slow digestion
(not that I would need them).

6) The first sacrifice results in Stormbringer gift.

7) I found another bag of holding in the Mines (at this moment I have
no idea how lucky find this is!)

8) As a true chaotic I murdered all the watchmen and shopkeepers and
looted their shops (not much really, but magic lamp).

9) In the main dungeon I continued my bloodthirsty massacre of
shopkeepers, including large shop full of scrolls.

10) Got genocide from a dlvl 7 throne: genocided disenchanters.

11) On dlvl 14 I found another wand of wishing

12) Another two genocides from d dlvl 18 throne: mind flayers and
master mind flayers.

13) Medusa and Castle were nominal and I reached VoTD. When I was
establishing my stash there
I accidentaly put my wand of cancellation into my bag of holding, that
contained everything I had: three wands of wishing (13 wishes in
them), every single scroll, most of the rings, magic marker, extra
tools and special purpose armor (levitation boots, water walking
boots, oilskin). My perfect winning game was in tatters and future
prospects were not good. As I couldn't get past Castle trapdoors, the
only option was to go to Gehennom and hope for the best.

14) Three levels into Gehennom I found cursed -2 levitation boots, so
I turned back and went to my dlvl 10 stash. The stash contained my
extra bag of holding; I also identified amulet of ESP and ring of
protection from shape changers (very useful for rogue quest which is
full of chameleons).

15) I have gone to my Quest: the idea was to use my magic lamp to wish
for the ring of polymorph control and use tins of chameleon meat as
polymorph source -- in case I need to phase undiggable walls of the
ultimate quest level. On the way down I accidentally ate leprechaun
corpse and contracted teleportitis.

16) Of course, I fell into a different part of the Master Assassin's
stronghold, so I rubbed my magic lamp and got hostile djinni -- I
forgot that my lamp is not blessed! Fortunately, I could get out with
one randomly found cursed scroll of teleportation, but I had no means
of repeating my attempts to get to Master Assassin.

17) I had lot of scrolls of teleportation (deathdrops in Rogue quest
seem to be strongly biased towards them), but no way to confuse myself
to get levelport. I went to the Assassin's Guild Hall and waited for
about 3000 turns to get forgotten spell. Meanwhile I kept killing
nymphs, leprechauns and nagas and collected gold and loot.

18) After I got confusion on demand I went to Master Assassin and
zapped him with wand of death, taking no chances (the problem with MA
is that he teleports to upstairs where you cannot readily reach him).
With the Master Key of Thievery my teleportitis got under control and
I could clear the upper levels of loot and get out of quest.

19) I returned to my stash, sorted my loot and used all the potions I
collected in Quest to make new batch of holy water.

20) With blessed BoH I moved my stash to VoTD and proceeded mapping
Gehennom. I managed to upgrade my divination skill to "skilled", so
spell of magic mapping got to usable 34% failure rate. I also used
stack of 10 blessed potions of object detection (from all the nymphs
in the Quest) to quickly find useful stuff. I genocided all L (the
only scroll of genocide I found).

21) At Vlad's I got the usual amulet of life saving and water walking
boots, but the throne just vanished in puff of logic the first time I
sat on it. Sigh. A wish would be most welcome.

22) I returned to Orcus Town, killed its master and looted the shops.
I got ring of free action and two other uncursed rings I could not
identify (no identify scrolls and no way to write them). I BUC tested
and read four spellbooks I got at Vlad's, but none of them was
identify. Too bad. On the bright side, I also identified, that one of
the potions of water I found is cursed. Great for cursing all those
scrolls of teleportation and also a potion of gain level.

23) Returned to Minetown for candles and then to dlvl 10 altar (the
only aligned random generated altar in the whole game!) for more
sacrificing. I did not manage to get crowned.

24) Returning to VoTD, I accidentally attacked priest of Moloch.
Luckily, my only unidentified scroll was taming, so I made him
peaceful again.

25) I went to the Wizard's Tower and cleared the lower two levels. I
got three potions of gain level (great for Moloch's Sanctum), another
ring and amulet and a wand of enlightenment (so I could actually
identify those rings and amulets). I levelported back to VoTD to
process the loot. Unfortunately, no amulet of reflection and no ring
of conflict. The most useful thing was +1 ring increase damage.

26) Gone on to kill Rodney, but wand of death kept missing, so I just
whacked him with my Stormbringer. In Moloch's Sanctum I ended against
the wall with the hidden door, so I spent rather short time there.

27) Run up to the planes was relatively smooth, only two Rodney
visitations.

28) For the planes, the strategy was to use crystal ball to find the
portal. On Earth, there was no trouble. On Air, I meleed 3 or 4 air
elementals without much trouble (half physical damage is great) - I
used quaffed potions of levitation, since my only means of levitation
were -2 boots. Plane of Fire was very easy, but Water was what I was
really afraid of, since I couldn't genocide the sea monsters. I used
my levitation boots, but that meant no speed and lowered AC (to -26,
still comfortable). As to ward off drowning attacks, I was using
grease. Surprisingly, the Plane of Water turned out completely
uneventful, in part to my ability to cast detect monster and avoid
krakens. Astral wasn't very difficult and the second altar was the
right one. I did not use conflict (since I had none).

